    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71705462\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\"><p>We live in a society where cacophony and clattering are the norm while serenity remains a mute spectator. The other day, I was travelling with my family on a train from Mangaluru to Coimbatore. We were keenly looking forward to this trip as hardly do we get a chance to spend seven continuous hours of “family time” without any errands, visitors, or gadgets.</p><p>The chair car made sure that we did not doze off on the pretext of reading as it conventionally occurs in sleeper coaches. The air-conditioned coach had well-maintained chairs and appeared reasonably spic and span despite the colossal number of passengers it handles every day.</p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- November 22, 2026 05:30 am IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71705462\" data-title=\"In decibels they compete\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/in-decibels-they-compete/article71705462.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-fac74a5b478f3cebc96c8f21-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/open-page/in-decibels-they-compete/article71705462.ece');\">\n                Copy link  \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"email\"><a href=\"mailto:?subject=In%20decibels%20they%20compete&amp;amp;body=Check%20out%20this%20link%20https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fopinion%2Fopen-page%2Fin-decibels-they-compete%2Farticle71705462.ece\" target=\"_self\">\n       