    "content_text": "We live in a society where cacophony and clattering are the norm while serenity remains a mute spectator. The other day, I was travelling with my family on a train from Mangaluru to Coimbatore. We were keenly looking forward to this trip as hardly do we get a chance to spend seven continuous hours of “family time” without any errands, visitors, or gadgets.\nThe chair car made sure that we did not doze off on the pretext of reading as it conventionally occurs in sleeper coaches. The air-conditioned coach had well-maintained chairs and appeared reasonably spic and span despite the colossal number of passengers it handles every day.\nPublished\n- November 22, 2026 05:30 am IST\nCopy link\nEmail\nFacebook\nTwitter\nTelegram\nLinkedIn\nWhatsApp\nReddit\nREAD LATER\nSEE ALL\nRemove",
