    "image_url": null,
    "image_caption": null,
    "content_html": "<div class=\"articlebodycontent col-xl-9 col-lg-12 col-md-12 col-sm-12 col-12\" id=\"content-body-71725465\"><div class=\"schemaDiv\" id=\"schemaDiv\"><p><i>(This is the latest edition of the Political Line newsletter curated by Varghese K. George. The Political Line newsletter is India’s political landscape explained every week. You can subscribe here to get the newsletter in your inbox every Friday.)</i></p><p>The ruling BJP leaves no opportunity to underscore its politics for tribespeople. The BJP elected the first tribal President of India, Droupadi Murmu, who also happens to be the first tribal woman to hold the highest office in the country. Under the BJP, India started observing Janjatiya Gaurav Divas (Tribal Pride Day) on November 15, the birth anniversary of Birsa Munda, a prominent tribal leader. </p><p>Prime Minister Narendra Modi paid floral tributes at Birsa Munda’s statue in the Parliament complex. Leaders of the BJP said Congress leader Rahul Gandhi’s absence was a sign of his lack of concern for tribal people. Mr. Gandhi was attending the Bharat Summit in Hyderabad, which is a Congress event backed by the Telangana State government. <a href=\"\" target=\"_self\">The BJP thought the conference was “anti-India”.</a> </p><p>Birsa Munda died in British police custody at the age of 24, in 1900, after he mobilised his Munda tribe in present-day Jharkhand. He was influenced by Christian missionaries in the early years, but later left that to fight for the protection of indigenous rights. </p><p>Tribespeople till today revere him as Dharti Aba or Father of the Earth. He founded the Birsait faith, and led the Ulgulan, the Great Tumult rebellion against British colonial rule and exploitative zamindari landlords to protect tribal land, forests, and self-rule (Abua Raj). His movement forced the British to pass the protective Chotanagpur Tenancy Act of 1908. It is important to recall what Munda represented. The pomp and politics around the commemoration<b> </b>of his memory does not merely overlook that, but also appears a design to erase his legacy of efforts to protect tribal rights. </p></div><div class=\"articleblock-container\" id=\"arthardpv\"></div><div class=\"update-publish-time article-published-time-end\"><p class=\"publish-time-new\"> Published <span>- November 20, 2026 09:02 pm IST</span></p></div><div class=\"comments-shares share-page flex print-hide\" data-artid=\"71725465\" data-title=\"Pride and Rights of Tribals\" data-url=\"https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/political-line-newsletter-pride-and-rights-of-tribals/article71725465.ece\"><div class=\"left\"><div class=\"share\"><button class=\"btn share-btn\" data-ga-labelclick=\"ArticleShare\"></button><ul class=\"share-list bottom\" style=\"display: none;\"><li class=\"copy-link\" data-cf-modified-8f77a868aba9fe3fca1347fd-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; copytext('https://www.thehindu.com/opinion/political-line-newsletter-pride-and-rights-of-tribals/article71725465.ece');\">\n                Copy link  \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"email\"><a href=\"mailto:?subject=Pride%20and%20Rights%20of%20Tribals&amp;amp;body=Check%20out%20this%20link%20https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fopinion%2Fpolitical-line-newsletter-pride-and-rights-of-tribals%2Farticle71725465.ece\" target=\"_self\">\n                    Email     \n                                \n                </a></li><li class=\"facebook\" data-cf-modified-8f77a868aba9fe3fca1347fd-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__cfRLUnblockHandlers) return false; openShareLink('https://www.facebook.com/sharer/sharer.php?u=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.thehindu.com%2Fopinion%2Fpolitical-line-newsletter-pride-and-rights-of-tribals%2Farticle71725465.ece&amp;t=Pride%20and%20Rights%20of%20Tribals')\">\n                Facebook   \n                        \n            </li><li class=\"twitter\" data-cf-modified-8f77a868aba9fe3fca1347fd-=\"\" onclick=\"if (!window.__